tients for patient centred approach to consultation in primary care: observational study</article-title><source>British Medical Journal</source><year>2001</year><month>2</month><day>24</day><volume>322</volume><issue>7284</issue><fpage>468</fpage><lpage>72</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11222423</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="r32"><label>32</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bond</surname><given-names>MR</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Patients experience of pain</article-title><source>Pharmacology &#x00026; therapeutics</source><year>1981</year><volume>12</volume><issue>3</issue><fpage>563</fpage><lpage>73</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7025033</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="r33"><label>33</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bibby</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The management of chronic neck pain&#x02013;A retrospective survey of the patient journey using in-depth semi-structured interviews</article-title><source>Journal of Orthopaedic Nursing</source><year>2006</year><volume>10</volume><fpage>25</fpage><lpage>32</lpage></element-citation></ref><ref id="r34"><label>34</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Holzemer</surname><given-names>WL</given-names></name><name><surname>Henry</surname><given-names>SB</given-names></name><name><surname>Reilly</surname><given-names>CA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Assessing and managing pain in AIDS care. The patient perspective</article-title><source>Journal of the Association of Nurses in AIDS Care</source><year>1998</year><volume>9</volume><issue>1</issue><fpage>22</fpage><lpage>30</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9436165</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="r35"><label>35</label><element-citation public